{% doc %}
  PDP delivery information block (free-UK-delivery cutover, 2026-07-03):
  honest sticker price + transparent delivery BEFORE checkout. UK delivery is
  free on EVERY order - checkout charges GBP 0 for the UK on all shipping
  profiles (the item's freight is baked into the sticker by PawScout's pricing
  rule), so there is no threshold and no standard rate to disclose.

  Delivery estimate: PawScout writes a per-product order->door range (calendar
  days, e.g. "6-21") into supplier.delivery_days from the synced CJ logistics
  matrix. When present it's shown verbatim; when blank (stale / not yet synced)
  a conservative static window is shown. Rule: only surface what is real and
  defensible - the synced figure when we have it, a conservative window otherwise.
  @param {product} product - Product being viewed
  @param {string} delivery_days - synced order-to-door range when fresh, blank when stale or absent
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  # delivery_days arrives from the caller (supplier-availability field 11): the synced
  # range when the supplier check is fresh, blank otherwise (PRD R4, decision 5b).
  comment
    Fallback bands (2026-07-06, owner-approved envelope: processing 1-3 +
    door transit + 2 days slack, customs rides inside CJ door transit):
    GB-warehoused 3-10, everything else 6-14. Only shown for a product the
    nightly has not stamped yet; origin picks the honest lane.
  endcomment
  assign fallback_days = '6-14'
  if product.metafields.supplier.origin.value == 'GB'
    assign fallback_days = '3-10'
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%} Three facts, one line EACH (owner clarification 2026-07-06):
    rows never wrap - compact markers instead of browser bullets, nowrap with
    a viewport-scaled font so every row stays a single line on phones. {%- endcomment -%}
<div class="delivery-info" aria-label="Delivery information">
  <ul class="di-rows">
    <li><strong>FREE UK delivery</strong>&nbsp;on every order</li>
    <li>Estimated {% if delivery_days != blank %}{{ delivery_days }}{% else %}{{ fallback_days }}{% endif %} days to your door</li>
    <li>14-day returns &middot; <a href="/policies/refund-policy">see our returns policy</a></li>
  </ul>
</div>
